{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/perf/budget.json","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-14T02:31:40.408460Z","id":"83a2543bcb5633dd4b9f1b963e4fdee6e72091fde7a697b1d3aaf8eb3b6b1d55","body":{"detail":"Measured 2026-10-13 on one idle Mac (AC power), CLAX_PERF_QUICK=1 npm run perf, main (579bdc8b) and rust-int (5fccef6b) alternating: main comment ready 99-100 ms in run 1 (failed, limit 86 at scale 1.00) and 91 ms in run 2 (passed, limit 94 at scale 1.09); rust-int 101-104 ms in four runs at scale 1.00-1.09 (failed) and 104-128 ms at scale 1.36-1.45 (failed on 128 vs 117). Cold ready latency is also at or over its 38 ms limit on both (39-41 ms). Logs: target/int/ttu-main-*.log and ttu-br-*.log in that worktree. Either the budget no longer matches this machine, or comment readiness regressed before main's tip; the branch adds roughly 3-10 ms on top.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":24},"end":{"line":31},"content_hash":"bdb9b4773ddf4cd164ffbfbeb2717bcfe8744d1cf5cd00d81b4975c37703047c"},"summary":"Time to usable's comment ready runs over its 86 ms darwin budget on main and on rust-int alike, the branch a few ms slower","tags":["perf","status:needs-decision","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/perf/bundle-budget.json","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T06:02:11.815194Z","id":"5ad3c5f8ab05006d60be365677ee7556e17b42a353875e335a37319751a4fcd0","body":{"detail":"The panel embeds the shell's Sidebar, ThreadCard and SendButton; the owner chip, the withheld label and the Send menu's grouping brought it to 65396 gzip bytes (from 65043), with the menu and the approval card moved into lazy chunks. The extension's own Send menu names (plan Task 23) have almost no room.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":15},"end":{"line":15},"content_hash":"935c259722638f24eea9dd631ad2e5f8cc1da6109229199e3b748da29265c76f"},"summary":"The extension panel is 140 bytes under its 65536 ceiling","tags":["task:23","bundle","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/perf/bundle-budget.json","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T06:22:22.164076Z","id":"ff328e16b94a81723262286df965f61e4eb3a5dd1c0f97ca35e60b70ba87c4ba","body":{"kind":"comment","references":"5ad3c5f8ab05006d60be365677ee7556e17b42a353875e335a37319751a4fcd0","summary":"Confirmed with both builds' scripts/bundle-size.mjs: extension panel 65043 gzip bytes at a2378555, 65396 at f7a89d53 (ceiling 65536); questions 15125 -> 15564, people 12525 -> 12587; artifact unchanged at 64069, which equals its budget. The panel embeds the shell's SendButton and its lazy SendMenu, so names and person groups reach the extension's Send menu once its agents carry name and person; the panel's link from an approval item to the shell's inbox (spec 2026-10-08 section 17) is the next code to land there. Recommendation: decide the panel ceiling before that work (for example 66560, with a note of what grew) rather than squeezing; the 140 bytes left will not hold a link component and its styles.","tags":["review","status:needs-decision","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/perf/bundle-budget.json","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T06:49:36.260982Z","id":"2c03296e1e23090fbcdd86127cab3e21dd0ce1138e46921239907b0abf128436","body":{"kind":"comment","references":"ff328e16b94a81723262286df965f61e4eb3a5dd1c0f97ca35e60b70ba87c4ba","summary":"After the round-1 fixes (bb547990) the extension panel measures 65526 of 65536 gzip bytes (10 left); the artifact entry measures 64062 of 64069, its Send default moved into the sidebar chunk.","tags":["bundle","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/perf/bundle-budget.json","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-15T03:40:37.891674Z","id":"ca2f1e9d1f8982634c233f3f36d8c5f2b825007457a5794e18be6e2eee744a14","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:a3ae32de","summary":"The owner raised extPanel to 66560 (874f36ab). With the panel's Send rule, the worker's approves-first lookup and the approval rows' link (a3ae32de), node web/scripts/bundle-size.mjs measures: panel 66388 of 66560, artifact 64062 of 64069 and gallery 27929 of 27960 (both unchanged from 086b92c8), questions 15608 of 16384.","supersedes":"5ad3c5f8ab05006d60be365677ee7556e17b42a353875e335a37319751a4fcd0","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/perf/bundle-budget.json","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-15T05:59:02.546920Z","id":"8653ded3974d2ab20916ce90da29649c32a3b18fa4e767b1c459629d978dddc4","body":{"detail":"Spec 2026-10-08-multi-agent-multi-person §23: the people module is lazy (16 KiB), gallery and artifact grow by at most 512 bytes, extPanel stays within 65,536. Measured at 09672011 (node web/scripts/bundle-size.mjs): panel 66,555 against 66,560 (raised in 874f36ab), artifact 64,062 against 64,069 (63,988 at the branch's base: 74 bytes over main, within the 512), people 13,636 against 16,384, gallery 27,929 against 27,960. Either the panel sheds about 1 KiB (for one, its Send menu and approval items loaded when first opened) or the spec's 65,536 is amended; the artifact entry needs room before its next change, up to main's size plus 512 once the branch is rebased and main's sizes measured again.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":15},"end":{"line":15},"content_hash":"bba27ecb5f1319da2af32bd259747e5f7245ba1bf7c1bc3fdbd2e87c31338ae2"},"summary":"extPanel's budget, 66,560 gzip bytes, is over spec §23's 65,536; the artifact entry has 7 bytes left","tags":["bundle","spec:23","status:needs-decision","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/perf/bundle-budget.json","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-14T12:34:33.800076Z","id":"5b1cd879b46b3c28d1a42687510efc263d42d6b73dc76166d32ea830e93e6302","body":{"detail":"Measured with web/scripts/bundle-size.mjs at 66d2a8f3: gallery 27915, artifact 64069 (exactly at budget). With hosted mode: gallery 28063 (the dynamic import of web/shell/src/hosted/SignIn.svelte in web/shell/src/gallery-main.ts), artifact 64174 (NO_VIEWER in web/shell/src/threads.ts and the guest_name_required check in web/shell/src/view/artifact-controller.ts submitDraft). `--record` never raises a budget, so the raise is the owner's call. A separate signin.html entry was tried and cost more (the Svelte runtime split into two shared chunks, gallery 28698).","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":3},"end":{"line":4},"content_hash":"22ba18f2fd9882bbc078f52c81a769741d83a1cbdbc951fea67e25b0a47d4354"},"suggested_fix":"Accept the raise, or move the sign-in pages out of the shell's bundles (server-rendered pages).","summary":"The gallery and artifact budgets were raised by hand for hosted mode (gallery 27960 to 28100, artifact 64069 to 64200)","supersedes":"f5acac29fd4ca2f1e5555e638561e97d1324b74586057a6115073d0311fc258b","tags":["status:needs-decision","hosted","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/perf/bundle-budget.json","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-14T12:35:23.268606Z","id":"69f7b606f4cc4bce3e4bfc15e8dd6765243f8927caa408a5ed150549be6f11f8","body":{"kind":"comment","references":"5b1cd879b46b3c28d1a42687510efc263d42d6b73dc76166d32ea830e93e6302","summary":"Changed since recorded: the budgets are now gallery 27960 and artifact 64243 (web/perf/bundle-budget.json:3-4). The artifact entry's was set to the live layers' measured size by 4f68518e; the gallery's is back at its pre-hosted value. The raise this record asks the owner about is no longer in the file.","tags":["session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/perf/bundle-budget.json","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-14T12:35:23.268733Z","id":"65344511aead0fc9df407cca5e428726e67dc64ebffaac6528f9d049ef8a2f65","body":{"kind":"comment","references":"5ad3c5f8ab05006d60be365677ee7556e17b42a353875e335a37319751a4fcd0","summary":"Changed since recorded: the extension panel's ceiling is 66560 gzip bytes (web/perf/bundle-budget.json:15), raised by 874f36ab at the owner's call. Proposed close: reason:obsolete.","tags":["session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/perf/bundle-budget.json","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-17T15:56:02.498969Z","id":"e2e655a2345a08b11a5996da4e81585b4f953862a0ceb9a3651725f1b63b3fde","body":{"detail":"Measured with node web/scripts/bundle-size.mjs (//web:bundle_size): extPanel 67,922 before, 66,027 after. web/extension/src/panel/Panel.svelte now imports Merge.svelte (the folded Merge pages section at the panel's foot) when it renders, as it already does InboxTab.svelte and Roster.svelte; the extension loads the chunk from its own files, so no network round trip is added. Moving web/shell/src/q/inbox-model.ts's notification text and URL filter out of the question module took about 125 more bytes off the panel. Reaching 65,536 would need another lazy part of about 500 bytes, for one Elsewhere.svelte (shown only when the site has threads on other pages) or SendButton's menu; the choice between that and amending the spec's 65,536 is still open.","kind":"comment","references":"8653ded3974d2ab20916ce90da29649c32a3b18fa4e767b1c459629d978dddc4","summary":"The panel measures 66,027 against its 66,560 budget, the budget unchanged; spec section 23's 65,536 is still 491 bytes away","tags":["bundle","spec:23","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/perf/bundle-budget.json","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-17T17:46:26.995763Z","id":"83eb0befefcaa3e8d35e7415c79c57cb1b6f1248c813f2e9680194ae0624cdf7","body":{"detail":"Before the thread and in-terminal question surfaces (parent of commit 3f7e040cd) it measured 16073: index 2901, open 10878, inbox-model 2294 (gzip -9 of the files web/scripts/bundle-size.mjs counts). With them it is 16746: the sidebar's thread check and on-demand hook in the index chunk, the in_terminal branch and the on-demand import (with its preload list) in the open chunk QuestionList.svelte shares, and inThread/closedLabel in model.ts. Everything else already loads on demand from web/shell/src/q/where.ts (TerminalCard, ThreadLinks, thread-slots), which the script does not count; loading everything eagerly measured 17691, and also put the extension panel over its budget (67251 > 66560; now 66394). The script calls this ceiling the spec's and never records it, so a raise belongs to the owner. Options: raise questions to 16896 or 17408, or ask for further cuts (for example moving byThread out of QuestionFeed, or moving the shared .qcard frame CSS), which save tens of bytes, not hundreds.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":5},"end":{"line":5},"content_hash":"edb8d25db9f80b9d4161f4375b98308d53ab2e317f39f3a593ad6a41286ad4d0"},"summary":"The question module measures 16746 gzip bytes against its 16384 ceiling, so //web:bundle_size fails","tags":["status:needs-decision","bundle","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/perf/bundle-budget.json","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-17T18:21:19.079589Z","id":"a800b624ee2291d23bb532c652d19d3ece9e0469836b45ce79c6cdcf4d062aa2","body":{"detail":"just web-test, //web:bundle_size: 'gzip bytes: ... questions 16828 ... panel 59195' and 'questions: 16828 gzip bytes, over its budget of 16384'. The 82 bytes beyond 16746 come from the thread link in the always-loaded QuestionCard (aboutLink in web/shell/src/q/model.ts) and QuestionList's thread prop. QuestionFeed.byThread moved into the on-demand ThreadQuestions. The panel fell from 66394 because its Page-view question block (web/extension/src/panel/PageQuestions.svelte) now loads on demand. The ceiling is unchanged.","kind":"comment","references":"83eb0befefcaa3e8d35e7415c79c57cb1b6f1248c813f2e9680194ae0624cdf7","summary":"At 0b7e4d15e the question module measures 16828 gzip bytes (444 over 16384) and the extension panel 59195 (budget 66560)","tags":["session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/perf/bundle-budget.json","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-18T20:01:13.074354Z","id":"bfc5fe5c7879bad0814800ce2948d258bf09dc219678753f4f0cecd43b185916","body":{"detail":"The gallery's unread summary (GallerySummary.svelte, with InboxRow.svelte, inbox-model.ts and open.ts, which only it and InboxPage use) left the q module (web/shell/src/q/index.ts no longer exports it). web/shell/src/ui/gallery-working.ts summary() imports it as its own chunk, and Gallery.svelte loadQ starts it on / in the same Promise.all as q() and the inbox page, so no request waits on another. The artifact view never showed it. bazel test //web:bundle_size: questions 13444, gallery 27834 (budget 27960, 27798 before), artifact 63627 (63612 before), extension panel 59306 (unchanged). bazel test //web:e2e_rest --test_arg=--grep=ask-where.spec: 24 passed, including the summary's terminal card and inbox row on /.","kind":"comment","references":"83eb0befefcaa3e8d35e7415c79c57cb1b6f1248c813f2e9680194ae0624cdf7","summary":"At 00d63fea2 the question module measures 13444 gzip bytes (16887 at d8bb21429), the budget unchanged at 16384","tags":["session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/perf/bundle-budget.json","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-18T20:01:13.074810Z","id":"b7cd30c21119e143c6b94bfaf973c7fc363b3af6189ba51def39ca26bf0a5b8a","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:00d63fea2","summary":"bazel test //web:bundle_size passes at 00d63fea2: questions 13444 gzip bytes against 16384","supersedes":"83eb0befefcaa3e8d35e7415c79c57cb1b6f1248c813f2e9680194ae0624cdf7","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/perf/bundle-budget.json","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T10:19:10.697502Z","id":"d039373ae8aa475c6fd4dea01498e57b97b9328454e5b68e66155f47fd13f719","body":{"detail":"node web/scripts/bundle-size.mjs on npm run build of git archives (gzip bytes). artifact: 64006 at 647958f22844^ and at 647958f22844 (W1's scroll code moved into the caps part by 647958f22844), 64180 at 647958f22844^ (+174, app mode's eager seams: the ?app=1 check and lazy host import, ArtifactMount.controller(), the controller's app hooks, Send label; 647958f22844, 647958f22844), 64370 at 647958f22844 (+190, db.artifact(id)'s eager seam; the cross-read code is a lazy chunk), 64370 at 647958f22844. Budget 64390 since 647958f22844 (overage 364 rounded up to 384; 20 bytes of headroom). eager bridge: 5462 at 647958f22844^, 5492 at 647958f22844 (+30, W1 long-press), 5493 at 647958f22844 (+1), 5508 at 647958f22844 (+15, the pick start's element description, 647958f22844). Budget 5565 since 647958f22844 (57 bytes of headroom). Inside their budgets and unchanged: caps part 8144 -> 8492 (W1 scroll report and restore, 647958f22844) -> 8691 (W3, 647958f22844), 82 bytes under 8773; comment part 10825 -> 11722 (W1 long-press) -> 11785 (W2 labels, 647958f22844), 36 bytes under 11821.","kind":"comment","span":{"start":{"line":4},"end":{"line":10},"content_hash":"59d05d05ba1f7453f5cbfd1e616f75fb3d9f36331c2bfba4b4df32ce0ea3f2b3"},"summary":"Why artifact, bridge and the caps and comment parts grew from W1 to W3 of the Flutter app plan, measured per commit","tags":["budget","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/perf/usable.perf.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T10:19:10.697702Z","id":"b1b478fbcb24df92c075295bea80c9e7b1f54995ae8a0144f2b661c353168e38","body":{"detail":"Every measured link in web/perf/usable.perf.ts is the browser's view. In the app's view (web/shell/src/artifact-main.ts) the host message ready that stops the app's say-usable timer is posted only after the host-*.js chunk loads, so a regression in that chunk's size or load order moves say-usable without failing any gate. The browser view's numbers were unchanged by app mode: interleaved CLAX_PERF_QUICK=1 runs with web/dist from 647958f22844^ and from 647958f22844 gave subdomain comment ready 84-102 ms and 85-105 ms at load average 9-10.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":115},"end":{"line":121},"content_hash":"71bda7919e5acd788c965c91cd7b3d6d28c2d33515ef8f081f0fc2b1a36b0517"},"suggested_fix":"Add an app-mode case to usable.perf.ts: open /a/<id>?app=1 with a stubbed window.ClaxHost (as web/e2e/app-host.ts does) and time link -> ready, with a recorded budget.","summary":"The time-to-usable gate opens /a/<id> without ?app=1: the Clax app's view, whose ready waits for the lazy host chunk, has no browser-side time budget","tags":["session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/perf/usable.perf.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T10:58:08.390341Z","id":"fc1351adb5996794e38f3aefe12ad2d43bbf7fbbfc55b71cdb40c5bffdacc417","body":{"detail":"The app's defended say-usable number stops on the shell's first `ready` (AppScreen.onReady, apps/clax_app/lib/ui/app_screen.dart:87-89), and on the phone app mode is the only view. That `ready` is posted from web/shell/src/app/host.ts:172 only once the lazy host chunk (dist/_clax/shell/host-*.js, 3677 gzip bytes at 647958f22844) has loaded, so its load and anything added before `ctl.app.welcome` move say-usable with no gate failing. Neither gate covers it: usable.perf.ts opens /a/<id> without ?app=1, and web/scripts/bundle-size.mjs:98 measures the artifact entry and the eager bridge but not the host chunk.","kind":"comment","references":"b1b478fbcb24df92c075295bea80c9e7b1f54995ae8a0144f2b661c353168e38","span":{"start":{"line":115},"end":{"line":121},"content_hash":"71bda7919e5acd788c965c91cd7b3d6d28c2d33515ef8f081f0fc2b1a36b0517"},"suggested_fix":"Add an app-mode case to usable.perf.ts: a context with a stubbed window.ClaxHost (as web/e2e/app-host.ts installs it) and the init call, open /a/<id>?app=1, time link -> first `ready` per frame mode, record its baseline and budget in web/perf/budget.json with CLAX_PERF_RECORD, and enforce it like commentReady.","summary":"Review of 647958f22844..647958f22844: this gap blocks the Flutter app's web track (plan Task W4), not a follow-up","tags":["review","perf","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/perf/usable.perf.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T12:18:50.264319Z","id":"d8ba30ecdfe48ae18f98751dde3869eb1c13967922b6b4a6b5dfc380489c1307","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:647958f22844","summary":"647958f22844 adds appReady (link -> the shell's first ready to a stubbed ClaxHost, init as soon as window.claxHost is defined) to every sample in both frame modes, with a darwin-arm64 baseline recorded by CLAX_PERF_RECORD=baseline at load average 5.6-6.0: subdomain 45 ms (budget 75), sandbox 42 ms (budget 72). Later CLAX_PERF_QUICK=1 runs measured app ready 41-48 ms against limits 75-92 in both modes, at load 4-21.","supersedes":"b1b478fbcb24df92c075295bea80c9e7b1f54995ae8a0144f2b661c353168e38","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/perf/bundle-budget.json","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T23:08:27.683825Z","id":"a0e78426df2a4980ad533491935a358b8d2e76be9518301592be19ac2ab0e566","body":{"detail":"node web/scripts/bundle-size.mjs (HEAD's copy) on npm run build of git archives of web/ and Cargo.toml, gzip bytes. Baseline 647958f22844 (the last budget raise). artifact: 64519 at 647958f22844 -> 64577 at 647958f22844 (+58, inspect view and composeArtifact seams) -> 64728 at 647958f22844 (+151, an attested press counted as the finger's arrival) -> 64751 at 647958f22844 (+23) -> 64756 at 647958f22844 (+5, the inspect frame name); unchanged through 647958f22844, 647958f22844, 647958f22844. eager bridge: 5508 at 647958f22844 -> 5915 at 647958f22844 (+407, the eager error ring) -> 5934 at 647958f22844 (+19, hold-then-drag chip) -> 5754 at 647958f22844 (-180, ring kept raw and only in the inspect frame). This eager growth (+246) loads on every page. app host: 3896 at 647958f22844 -> 3927 at 647958f22844 (+31, the animation-frame and visibility work of 647958f22844, 647958f22844, 647958f22844) -> 4952 at 647958f22844 (+1025, inspect, inspection, composeArtifact) -> 4999 at 647958f22844 (+47) -> 5062 at 647958f22844 (+63, held-press expiry and cancel) -> 6081 at 647958f22844 (+1019, the questions sheet) -> 6393 at 647958f22844 (+312, openQuestions by ID, closeQuestions, showing) -> 6400 at 647958f22844 (+7). comment part: 11823 at 647958f22844 -> 12310 at 647958f22844 (+487, hold then drag) -> 13036 at 647958f22844 (+726, the Comment chip offer). clip part: 15004 at 647958f22844 -> 16476 at 647958f22844 (+1472, settle, outline and renderViewport) -> 17336 at 647958f22844 (+860, faithfulClone placeholders and broken images). Budgets since 647958f22844: measured plus at least 32 bytes, rounded up to a multiple of 64 (artifact 64832, host 6464, bridge 5824, comment 13120, clip 17408). Inside unchanged budgets: questions 14194 -> 14347 (647958f22844 +142, 647958f22844 +11) under the 16384 ceiling; extension overlay 18988 -> 20268 (hold-then-drag in the shared bridge code, 647958f22844, 647958f22844) under 32768.","kind":"comment","span":{"start":{"line":4},"end":{"line":9},"content_hash":"b7be26657eb97721bfb164821092102a2e755e891145c8d0c133860b486f774c"},"summary":"Why artifact, app host, eager bridge and the comment and clip parts grew in round 2 of the Flutter app plan, measured per commit","tags":["budget","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/perf/bundle-budget.json","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T02:28:47.146938Z","id":"ab7a56c306f1cf189184c924b209da377e2ded837f6e380249f0b929b9da512f","body":{"detail":"Measured with web/scripts/bundle-size.mjs on two exports of HEAD at 647958f22844's parent tree with and without the device changes (target/v1-size/x and y): artifact 64836 -> 64994 (budget 64832), app host 6809 -> 7187 (budget 6464), eager bridge 5873 -> 5933 (budget 5824). The handler (caps/device.ts) is a lazy chunk; the artifact entry keeps only caps/device-link.ts, the availability rule and five lazy registry entries; the pending calls live in the app host chunk (app/host.ts deviceResult). The budgets need raising, or the other round 3 growth trimmed, before the bundle-size gate passes.","kind":"concern","summary":"The device capabilities add 158 gzip bytes to the artifact entry, 378 to app mode's host chunk and 60 to the eager bridge, over budgets others' round 3 changes had already reached","tags":["v1","perf","budget","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/perf/bundle-budget.json","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T02:40:02.280674Z","id":"8954310c0731f698dd0851a6fa0138b7077b2d434f7b233e672902c7784b42e4","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:647958f22844","summary":"Budgets raised in 647958f22844 to the measured sizes plus at least 32, rounded up to 64: artifact 65088 (65023), host 7296 (7245), bridge 6016 (5933), partCaps 9024 (8952). node web/scripts/bundle-size.mjs after scripts/build-web.sh reports no budget over.","supersedes":"ab7a56c306f1cf189184c924b209da377e2ded837f6e380249f0b929b9da512f","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/perf/bundle-budget.json","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-16T05:31:59.510051Z","id":"ab92f6e8e76c13fa36bbd518ff446ef06489f023229957e83a007fabbccaaf8f","body":{"detail":"app host 8826 -> 9088 for 9003: the page's route trail (8806 -> 8927 at 647958f22844) and the dropped-post notice, moved from the artifact entry to the host's ctl.app.dropped (artifact 65757 -> 65719). caps part 9664 -> 10048 for 9957: web/bridge/src/routes.ts (9588 -> 9875 at 647958f22844) and its traversal through the page's own entries (+71 at 647958f22844). Both load only in app mode. Rule: measured plus at least 32, rounded up to a multiple of 64.","kind":"comment","span":{"start":{"line":5},"end":{"line":10},"content_hash":"3ded60f1ceb62d06315088fdff5e83eebdc13f5ee2fd46498416d969abe87979"},"summary":"Why the app host and caps part budgets rose at 647958f22844, measured with node web/scripts/bundle-size.mjs after npm run build","tags":["perf","bundle-budget","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/perf/bundle-budget.json","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-16T14:09:51.196484Z","id":"a510e132d910bcb19aba9c81d12321b1715cb6320a598427ba469b3b375230ba","body":{"detail":"Spec 2026-10-08-multi-agent-multi-person §23: the people module is lazy (16 KiB), gallery and artifact grow by at most 512 bytes, extPanel stays within 65,536. Measured at cbf9530d346b (node web/scripts/bundle-size.mjs): panel 66,555 against 66,560 (raised in 1ffb8a506e09), artifact 64,062 against 64,069 (63,988 at the branch's base: 74 bytes over main, within the 512), people 13,636 against 16,384, gallery 27,929 against 27,960. Either the panel sheds about 1 KiB (for one, its Send menu and approval items loaded when first opened) or the spec's 65,536 is amended; the artifact entry needs room before its next change, up to main's size plus 512 once the branch is rebased and main's sizes measured again.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":16},"end":{"line":16},"content_hash":"bba27ecb5f1319da2af32bd259747e5f7245ba1bf7c1bc3fdbd2e87c31338ae2"},"summary":"extPanel's budget, 66,560 gzip bytes, is over spec §23's 65,536; the artifact entry has 7 bytes left","supersedes":"8653ded3974d2ab20916ce90da29649c32a3b18fa4e767b1c459629d978dddc4","tags":["bundle","spec:23","status:needs-decision","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/perf/bundle-budget.json","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-16T14:58:12.359219Z","id":"c516abb66b5a1546d20e48e4266e8f4549cc99da4f94949f33bffa275bf28779","body":{"detail":"Measured with node web/scripts/bundle-size.mjs after npm run build, at 647958f22844's parent and at 647958f22844. The artifact entry gains the home case in web/shell/src/caps/availability.ts, the served.home ask in web/shell/src/caps/host.ts and the registry entry; the caps part gains web/bridge/src/caps/home.ts (its method list). The artifact entry had 6 bytes of headroom before, so any eager gate for home exceeds it. Budgets follow the measure-plus-32-rounded-to-64 rule of earlier raises.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":4},"end":{"line":10},"content_hash":"51ba00c3716addb4d1524b871d18dd85eab146abdee6a9beed4a393834b35087"},"summary":"artifact and partCaps budgets raised for the home capability at 647958f22844 (artifact 65722 to 65752, caps part 9957 to 10070 gzip bytes)","tags":["perf","status:needs-decision","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/perf/bundle-budget.json","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T07:46:21.964280Z","id":"0d0f366f5df3f036415bcdcec2a4cfaa2475fced721ef460100904f63a4469a9","body":{"detail":"Measured by //web:bundle_size at 647958f22844 (gzip bytes: … parts: comment 14643, … caps 10918). The bridge's only source changes since the last budgets (647958f22844, 647958f22844) are web/bridge/src/describe.ts's nameOf and protocol.ts's KIND_WORDS, which anchor.ts's buildElementAnchor and buildRangeAnchor and area.ts's buildAreaAnchor now call to record Anchor.name at pick time (647958f22844), and one more HOME_METHODS entry (647958f22844). The caps part carries the naming through caps/comments.ts's buildElementAnchor. Budgets follow the measure-plus-32-rounded-to-64 rule of earlier raises (647958f22844). The owner decides between this raise and loading the naming as a chunk of its own.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":8},"end":{"line":10},"content_hash":"48d8e3ee6fa16dab6f495d5cad9048eac400cdac6bea98bd110850701ac978c8"},"summary":"partComment and partCaps budgets raised for anchor names at 647958f22844 (comment part 13854 to 14643, caps part 10070 to 10918 gzip bytes)","tags":["perf","status:needs-decision","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/perf/bundle-budget.json","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T08:42:15.037067Z","id":"dc24110ed92db79fed761f9fac554b6d1d5c98fb6010b5b5a402aafe2856c3bb","body":{"detail":"Measured by //web:bundle_size at 647958f22844: 'gzip bytes: … app host 8988, parts: … caps 11304'; with web/bridge/src/parts/caps.ts at its previous content the caps part measured 10918. The growth is web/bridge/src/chrome.ts (sampleChrome, reportChrome), which the caps part's app() starts on the app shell's welcome. The budget follows the measure-plus-32-rounded-to-64 rule of earlier raises (647958f22844). The eager bridge (6227) and the artifact bundle (65507, clax:chrome in BRIDGE_TYPES) stayed within their budgets. The owner decides between this raise and loading the sampler as a part of its own.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":10},"end":{"line":10},"content_hash":"5345718345d1cf46ebedc5beaae84ed7fe42fbdda879eac225c41b8d8f6b5a8c"},"summary":"partCaps budget raised for the page's edge-colour sampler at 647958f22844 (caps part 10918 to 11304 gzip bytes; budget 11008 to 11392)","tags":["perf","status:needs-decision","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/perf/bundle-budget.json","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T02:31:54.022953Z","id":"513b3306340cde8998f4b63317c67b4c59997a52df2d798e0d135e436a7f6dc8","body":{"detail":"Measured with bazelisk test //web:bundle_size at 647958f22844: gallery 29423 (budget 28096), artifact 67570 (budget 66048), app host 9158 (budget 9088). With the entries' and host.ts's changes of 647958f22844 reverted (conn-notice.ts and lifecycle.ts kept) the same gate measured gallery 27990, artifact 66127, app host 9121; artifact, app host and eager bridge (6308 of 6272) were already over. A browser runs only readEmbed and installTransport's early return; hostFetch, the chunking and the stream are dead weight there. Keeping only readEmbed and a waiting fetch in the entries and loading the rest by dynamic import in app mode would cut most of it, at the price of one more chunk before the first API call in the app.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":3},"end":{"line":4},"content_hash":"99176a25a178f2bbe5fe2c6f02970b4b329af65113e3badb14554567ec46f724"},"summary":"web/shell/src/transport.ts adds about 1.4 KB gzip to both the gallery and the artifact entries, which load it eagerly in a browser too","tags":["status:needs-decision","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/perf/bundle-budget.json","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T02:48:02.574448Z","id":"b904bd03c3f3888288c46a296b2495c5a79a5508adfa795818cee0b11841f012","body":{"detail":"Failure: bazelisk test //web:bundle_size at 647958f22844 prints 'gallery: 29423 gzip bytes, over its budget of 28096', 'artifact: 67570 ... 66048', 'host: 9158 ... 9088', 'bridge: 6308 ... 6272'.\nPer commit, measured with web/scripts/bundle-size.mjs over the package.json build of `git archive <commit> web Cargo.toml` (the same build gives 29423/67570/9158/6308 at 647958f22844, as Bazel does): 647958f22844^ artifact 66007, app host 8889, eager bridge 6227; 647958f22844 (clax:wait) 66018, 9041, 6268; 647958f22844 (the pick's `at`: bridge.ts box()/rect, pick.ts, composer-model.ts boxOf, host.ts inShell) 66098 (+80), 9121 (+80), 6307 (+39), all three over; 647958f22844 bridge 6308. 647958f22844 then adds gallery 27961 to 29423 (+1462), artifact +1472, app host +37: transport.ts loads eagerly in both browser entries, where only readEmbed and installTransport's early return run; connNotices in conn-notice.ts costs about 30 bytes and retrying's connNoticesOn check in lifecycle.ts 28 bytes in each entry. Record 513b3306 has the reverted measure.\nMeasured prototypes (scratch builds, not typechecked):\n(1) Transport out of the browser entries. A: the core's with_embed_meta (crates/clax-server/src/shell/boot.rs:397) also writes a classic <script> for a transport.js built as its own IIFE (1790 gzip bytes), which replaces fetch before any module runs, hides .conn-notice with a style it adds, and installs window.claxTransport {init, callResult, streamBlock, streamEnd}; entries, conn-notice.ts and lifecycle.ts as at 647958f22844^: gallery 27961, artifact 66098, app host 9121 when the app's Init calls claxTransport.init, 9140 when host.ts forwards the nonce. B: each entry tests the meta and boots after `import(\"./transport\")` in app mode: gallery 28053 (with the retrying check dropped), artifact 66187, and the gate's app host 10999 because it counts the transport chunk host.ts imports (9190 counted as already loaded); the app gains a sequential chunk load before boot.\n(2) The pick place: the controller keeps the raw `at` and app/host.ts validates it with boxOf (only the app reads it), boxOf written as `[x, y, w, h].every(Number.isFinite) && w >= 0 && h >= 0`, pick.ts posts `at` unconditionally, bridge.ts derives box() from a rect(DOMRect) it also uses for pickArea: with A, artifact 66023, eager bridge 6292, app host 9167.\n(3) Eager bridge, 20 over after (2): PickFlow and the pick hooks into the comment part: eager bridge 5788, comment part 15188 against its 14720 (a move between budgets, not a raise of their sum); or post no `at` and place the app's composer from the shell's anchors answer (bridge about 6269, not measured end to end).\n(4) App host, 79 over after (2): the inspect view's handlers (inspect, runTests, runMigration, journalAck, restoreJournal in app/host.ts) in a chunk of their own: a stub of them measured app host 8142 and artifact 65887, an upper bound on the saving.","kind":"blocker","span":{"start":{"line":3},"end":{"line":7},"content_hash":"1ef17899df25817b31b41825a246bd1d5641ba33669620c9b8dd13dc0c74fa15"},"suggested_fix":"(1)A, (2), (4), and (3) by the owner's choice between the budget move and dropping `at` from the bridge; no budget raised.","summary":"//web:bundle_size fails on four entries at 647958f22844: the transport loads in browsers, and 647958f22844 had already put the artifact, app host and eager bridge over","tags":["perf","review","status:needs-decision","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/perf/bundle-budget.json","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T02:48:02.575708Z","id":"0a9c910536ee776f8741d577d3529017d4c8eac24248bfba9c6cabb584ad5979","body":{"detail":"Gallery and artifact: 27961 and 66098 with transport.js as a classic script the core writes after the meta (1790 gzip bytes of its own); 28053 and 66187 with each entry importing the transport dynamically in app mode. The plan for all four failing entries is in the blocker on web/perf/bundle-budget.json:3:7.","kind":"comment","references":"513b3306340cde8998f4b63317c67b4c59997a52df2d798e0d135e436a7f6dc8","span":{"start":{"line":3},"end":{"line":4},"content_hash":"99176a25a178f2bbe5fe2c6f02970b4b329af65113e3badb14554567ec46f724"},"summary":"Measured the ways out: a core-written transport script leaves both entries at 647958f22844^'s sizes; a dynamic import costs 92 and 89 bytes","tags":["review","perf","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/perf/bundle-budget.json","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T03:57:37.105302Z","id":"aa393abbcb0903475069df88c0e23b1c5c7d82d30ba1719c7d5cf00cd2a64afb","body":{"kind":"comment","references":"b904bd03c3f3888288c46a296b2495c5a79a5508adfa795818cee0b11841f012","summary":"The owner chose this path on 2026-10-19: transport.js written by the core (option (1)A), boxOf in app/host.ts, no `at` in the bridge with the app's composer placed from the shell's anchors answer, the inspect view's handlers in a chunk, answers bound to the load's nonce, the nonce in the document, and subscribe carrying lastEventId.","tags":["status:decided","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/perf/bundle-budget.json","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T03:57:37.105699Z","id":"3c81a2c647ad414d7af3fde606e63c06c7f76d9c663c0526b0c007fe2fbaade9","body":{"kind":"comment","references":"513b3306340cde8998f4b63317c67b4c59997a52df2d798e0d135e436a7f6dc8","summary":"The owner chose this path on 2026-10-19: transport.js written by the core (option (1)A), boxOf in app/host.ts, no `at` in the bridge with the app's composer placed from the shell's anchors answer, the inspect view's handlers in a chunk, answers bound to the load's nonce, the nonce in the document, and subscribe carrying lastEventId.","tags":["status:decided","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/perf/bundle-budget.json","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T03:57:37.106599Z","id":"9110be5abcc26f7fa2de4a71c0409461571f40dd023f39bee577a8061cd5d587","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:647958f22844","summary":"Fixed by 647958f22844 (transport.js, entries back), 647958f22844 (no `at` in the bridge), 647958f22844 (inspect chunk). Bundle gate (bazelisk test //web:bundle_size, passing) at 647958f22844: gallery 27961 of 28096, artifact 66045 of 66048, app host 8252 of 9088, eager bridge 6268 of 6272, transport 2015 of its own new budget 2038; no budget raised.","supersedes":"b904bd03c3f3888288c46a296b2495c5a79a5508adfa795818cee0b11841f012","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/perf/bundle-budget.json","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T03:57:37.251694Z","id":"e9247e5501e2fa4e895cb3f6d7405394a77d9e88054ba078f200e7886f9d9bf3","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:647958f22844","summary":"Fixed by 647958f22844: the transport is /_clax/transport.js, a classic script only an embedded core's shell documents load; Bundle gate (bazelisk test //web:bundle_size, passing) at 647958f22844: gallery 27961 of 28096, artifact 66045 of 66048, app host 8252 of 9088, eager bridge 6268 of 6272, transport 2015 of its own new budget 2038; no budget raised.","supersedes":"513b3306340cde8998f4b63317c67b4c59997a52df2d798e0d135e436a7f6dc8","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/perf/bundle-budget.json","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T04:04:06.183223Z","id":"b927a8b7872f03dea86daff28bab88b0cf81f0b6821e7f4aca6a95b5315603b8","body":{"detail":"bazelisk test //web:bundle_size on flutter-app at 647958f22844: gallery 27961/28096 (135 left), artifact 66045/66048 (3), app host 8252/9088 (836), eager bridge 6268/6272 (4), transport 2015/2038 (23). The artifact budget has been raised by hand at least four times (647958f22844, 647958f22844, 647958f22844, 4f68518e; records c516abb6, a510e132, 5b1cd879), so 3 bytes is not headroom but the last raise's exact size; --record (web/scripts/bundle-size.mjs) never raises. The bridge's 4 bytes are after 647958f22844 removed the pick's `at`, so it was tighter still. 647958f22844 added the app's anchors to ArtifactController.resolveAll (in the artifact entry) for app mode alone. Candidates, unmeasured: move app-mode-only branches out of the controller (the app hook's anchors()/welcome() merging and dbJournal, which only app/host.ts and app/inspect.ts set) behind the app hook so the entry carries only the call sites; and find what of the ThemeSwitch chunk (18467 gzip bytes, shared with the gallery) the artifact view never renders, with a sourcemap build of vite.shell.config.ts.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":4},"end":{"line":7},"content_hash":"6e634d5090aab86e56b49e8c1a28602808403607c67ec8b7130c2a50a0737751"},"summary":"The artifact entry has 3 gzip bytes of budget left and the eager bridge 4: any change to either fails the gate or raises its budget by hand again","tags":["status:needs-decision","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/perf/bundle-budget.json","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T06:03:52.031366Z","id":"46d3532990a0a39a9449fecc7f9b97d3a844ebe05a9a648a01abf4388fc2f026","body":{"kind":"comment","references":"b927a8b7872f03dea86daff28bab88b0cf81f0b6821e7f4aca6a95b5315603b8","summary":"Owner's decision (2026-10-19): no budget raises; make the headroom by structural savings instead. Measured with a sourcemap build of vite.shell.config.ts: the ThemeSwitch chunk (18455 gzip) is Svelte's runtime (batch, boundary, each, effects: mount always uses boundary) plus lifecycle, api, ThemeSwitch.svelte and theme-model, all of which the artifact view renders or runs, so nothing came out of it; the app-mode-only controller branches (app hook, appFocus, dbJournal) are a few hundred minified bytes. The saving taken is the artifact capability's handler as a lazy chunk (647958f22844, as the device capabilities' are): artifact 66045 -> 64777 of 66048. The eager bridge's part loader tables are built from the part list (647958f22844): 6268 -> 6172 of 6272. Moving scroll-to into the comment part saved 196 bridge bytes but put the comment part 85 over its budget, so it was not taken.","tags":["session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/perf/bundle-budget.json","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T06:03:52.031643Z","id":"ec4b8f534ceaa740886ecf3da9dae08e92f7677d61a51f70a8b6b347ed67d560","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:647958f22844","summary":"Headroom made with no budget raised (647958f22844, 647958f22844). bazelisk test //web:bundle_size at 647958f22844 passed: gallery 27960 of 28096, artifact 64777 of 66048 (1271 left, 1.9%), app host 8379 of 9088, eager bridge 6172 of 6272 (100 left, 1.6%), transport 2015 of 2038, parts comment 14643 of 14720, clip 17351 of 17408, caps 11343 of 11392; web/perf/bundle-budget.json unchanged.","supersedes":"b927a8b7872f03dea86daff28bab88b0cf81f0b6821e7f4aca6a95b5315603b8","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/perf/bundle-budget.json","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T14:29:43.676336Z","id":"24d927a6406918a8608a687ced0e4e088fe5812428c7219131985a6997dfb606","body":{"detail":"web/shell/src/transport.ts gained the callResultChunk receiver, a settle helper shared with callResult, and fromBase64 over several parts (commit 647958f22844). The budget had 16 bytes of headroom, so any chunked-answer receiver goes over it. Raise accepted or the receiver trimmed: the owner's call.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":8},"end":{"line":8},"content_hash":"f9a6e774bf47099fe76ec22b29b0fd476876c652700304ed5c410f0b5d07d115"},"summary":"The transport budget rises from 2038 to 2192 gzip bytes for callResultChunk (measured 2022 before, 2192 after, bazelisk test //web:bundle_size)","tags":["bundle-budget","status:needs-decision","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/perf/bundle-budget.json","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T14:48:36.059673Z","id":"3445205673aef9dfaf41ce74b0d3986a24857705f0542488ed6d402f836929fa","body":{"detail":"Each variant was built as vite.transport.config.ts builds it and gzipped at level 9 as web/scripts/bundle-size.mjs does (HEAD rebuilt that way gives 2191, the same as bazelisk test //web:bundle_size). Before 647958f22844: 2022. HEAD (callResultChunk, settle, the parts map, fromBase64 over an array): 2191. Parts folded into callResult with an array kept on the call's Pending entry: 2074. The same with the parts' base64 joined as one string (every part but the last a multiple of 3 bytes, so the base64 texts concatenate into the whole body's): 2043. That plus `new URL(input instanceof Request ? input.url : String(input), origin)` in hostFetch (String of a URL is its href, so the `instanceof URL` branch is redundant): 2031. The fold, in transport.ts: Pending gains `more?: string`; callResult does `const b64 = (p.more ?? \"\") + r.body64; if (r.more) return void (p.more = b64);` before calls.delete, and decodes b64 instead of r.body64. A node run of that build reassembled a 3 * 786432 + 7 byte body sent as three `{body64, more: true}` parts and a last `{status, headers, body64}` byte for byte. The relay sends parts of 3 << 18 bytes (exactly 1 MiB of base64 each). Avoiding chunking altogether is not advised: the core answers up to 96 MiB, about 128 Mi base64 characters in one runJavaScript, which Android carries to the renderer as one UTF-16 IPC message of about 256 MiB (Chromium's Mojo caps a message at 256 MiB by default; not measured here), and both platforms copy the string several times on the way. Raising the cap to 8 MiB, as the request side's CHUNKED_OVER, would chunk fewer answers but still needs the receiver.","kind":"comment","references":"24d927a6406918a8608a687ced0e4e088fe5812428c7219131985a6997dfb606","summary":"Measured: the receiver fits the old 2038 budget with no raise, at 2031 gzip bytes, by folding the parts into callResult and saving 12 bytes elsewhere","tags":["review","task:15","bundle-budget","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/perf/bundle-budget.json","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T17:42:31.110334Z","id":"0e3f3afc55b425570acfb01f21cf2385fb10e442c97734d851f3916aac9df7f1","body":{"kind":"comment","references":"24d927a6406918a8608a687ced0e4e088fe5812428c7219131985a6997dfb606","summary":"Decision (owner, 2026-10-20): fold the parts into callResult. Every part but the last goes as callResult(nonce, id, {body64, more: true}), each a multiple of 3 bytes so the base64 joins; the last is the ordinary callResult with status and headers; the parts are kept on the call's pending entry, so an abort frees them; callResultChunk and hostFetch's instanceof URL branch are removed; the transport budget goes back to 2038.","tags":["status:decided","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/perf/bundle-budget.json","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T17:42:31.161208Z","id":"e9b16ee63205f55644e36a73013b87a4b8da5b31f6ccfe64369b5d2d6b73b619","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:647958f22844","summary":"Fixed as decided: the transport is 2037 gzip bytes against its restored budget of 2038 (bazelisk test //web:bundle_size: PASSED, 'transport 2037'); callResultChunk is gone from web/shell/src/transport.ts","supersedes":"24d927a6406918a8608a687ced0e4e088fe5812428c7219131985a6997dfb606","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/perf/bundle-budget.json","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T18:48:23.470803Z","id":"717d283bc0cb09f010acc169dec8ca86f8466224ce7586bb137150fc48f808b7","body":{"detail":"Main measured exactly 28159 gzip bytes against a budget of 28159, so any gallery change needs room. The card's by-line gained `p.a.brief?.by ||` (web/shell/src/ui/GalleryCard.svelte), 13 gzip bytes after trying shorter forms. The alternatives are a chip from the lazy gallery module (cardMarkers), which would still read 'command line' in the by-line, or finding 13 bytes elsewhere in the gallery entry.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":3},"end":{"line":3},"content_hash":"65bc77da077a9dd2aba522a02928bbbf96de8af6ffa3ef626701cfb384443519"},"summary":"The gallery's bundle budget was raised 13 bytes (28159 to 28172) for the gallery card naming who started an artifact from a brief","tags":["status:needs-decision","bundle","session:claude-code:d1f51555-8e8f-4c11-acd6-673f773ac34d"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/perf/bundle-budget.json","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T18:06:41.266877Z","id":"28f0e3b73a4e9701d32f13e35b03b0f710869021241aa2f18aae816a3c5117a6","body":{"detail":"The thread drawer (web/shell/src/ui/SidebarIsland.svelte, DrawerChrome.svelte, web/shell/artifact.html's clax-drawer script) brought the artifact entry from 63,997 to 64,241 gzip bytes, measured by web/scripts/bundle-size.mjs under bazelisk test //web:bundle_size. Everything else about the drawer was moved into the sidebar's lazy chunk to fit; the next eager addition to the artifact entry will fail the gate unless the budget is raised or something eager is made lazy.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":4},"end":{"line":4},"content_hash":"32dc2973c8ce2aff5dab4f49139a0b61663391620f3ba7116a4c5d265bb5703e"},"summary":"The artifact entry has 2 gzip bytes left under its budget (64,241 of 64,243) after the thread drawer's layouts","tags":["budget","session:claude-code:d1f51555-8e8f-4c11-acd6-673f773ac34d"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/perf/bundle-budget.json","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T18:41:00.787525Z","id":"a1095c01bc26e0d242969e554d529a634a31ef0fae70c94f85ae62c4ff8201eb","body":{"kind":"comment","references":"28f0e3b73a4e9701d32f13e35b03b0f710869021241aa2f18aae816a3c5117a6","span":{"start":{"line":4},"end":{"line":4},"content_hash":"32dc2973c8ce2aff5dab4f49139a0b61663391620f3ba7116a4c5d265bb5703e"},"summary":"Now 64,237 of 64,243 (6 bytes left): the head script applies only the layout and docked sizes, and the docked drawer's flex: none moved to the lazy chunk (DrawerChrome.svelte).","tags":["session:claude-code:d1f51555-8e8f-4c11-acd6-673f773ac34d"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/perf/bundle-budget.json","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T20:08:29.138977Z","id":"838adb2fd2d5a0526a64724f2d513e458d4142e158faee8b1e1aa50e83a9a8b2","body":{"detail":"Measured by bazel test //web:bundle_size at d62f346eb. The budget is unchanged.","kind":"comment","references":"28f0e3b73a4e9701d32f13e35b03b0f710869021241aa2f18aae816a3c5117a6","summary":"With comment Markdown and the brief line merged in, the artifact entry measured 64,728; PromptDialog.svelte is now a lazy chunk (web/shell/src/ui/StageIsland.svelte), and the entry is 63,942 of 64,243 (301 bytes left)","tags":["session:claude-code:d1f51555-8e8f-4c11-acd6-673f773ac34d"]}}
