{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/perf/bundle-budget.json","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T00:25:10.425272Z","id":"f92c2790ce96a3165b773a829005785103f4f41dbe70c6a08100d5063a519595","body":{"detail":"Measured with node web/scripts/bundle-size.mjs after npm run build: artifact 64243 (budget was 64069), eager bridge 5548 (was 5501; 5462 at 66d2a8f3), comment part 11273 (its budget 11821 kept), the new live part 4197 (budget 4616). The budgets for artifact and bridge are set to those sizes. The drawing, the pointer reports and the quote highlight are the bridge's live part (web/bridge/src/live.ts, loaded by web/bridge/src/live-hook.ts for the first open quote or the first clax:peers naming someone or saying here); the tags, writers, socket and colours load after the first paint with presence (web/shell/src/view/presence-live.ts). What is left: in the entry, the controller's hand-off (web/shell/src/view/artifact-controller.ts startLive, about 70 bytes; react, hello and left, about 20; the clax:cursor/peer-at case, about 19; the open threads' highlight flag, about 13); in the eager bridge, the live part's loader (about 13), the clax:peers case and its SHELL_TYPES entry (about 12), the quotes call in resolveAll (about 12) and making the hook and handing it to comment mode. Removing each was measured; none of it can move to a lazy chunk without the entry or the bridge keeping a call to it. Options: keep these budgets; or refuse and drop a layer (the quote highlight saves about 12 bridge bytes and 13 entry bytes).","kind":"comment","span":{"start":{"line":4},"end":{"line":6},"content_hash":"0e2e62240da64688f79b1984e9362192eb5819fd2a0beaada28d37fb73c79752"},"summary":"Raise or refuse: the live layers' bundle growth (artifact +174, eager bridge +47 gzip bytes over their old budgets; the comment part is back under its own)","supersedes":"07e0eb7aa1b8f5aeeb264e39703f6ba9f01386530457b1f22eac42642f3e0301","tags":["live-layers","status:needs-decision","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347","session:claude-code:d1f51555-8e8f-4c11-acd6-673f773ac34d"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/perf/bundle-budget.json","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T05:11:04.354017Z","id":"c0e6fdcbbf6e0ad263d1235c883c2ff4ccc468f3227f1b7febc0d72b02b5820c","body":{"detail":"Measured with node web/scripts/bundle-size.mjs after npm run build: artifact 64243 (budget was 64069), eager bridge 5548 (was 5501; 5462 at 66d2a8f3), comment part 11273 (its budget 11821 kept), the new live part 4197 (budget 4616). The budgets for artifact and bridge are set to those sizes. The drawing, the pointer reports and the quote highlight are the bridge's live part (web/bridge/src/live.ts, loaded by web/bridge/src/live-hook.ts for the first open quote or the first clax:peers naming someone or saying here); the tags, writers, socket and colours load after the first paint with presence (web/shell/src/view/presence-live.ts). What is left: in the entry, the controller's hand-off (web/shell/src/view/artifact-controller.ts startLive, about 70 bytes; react, hello and left, about 20; the clax:cursor/peer-at case, about 19; the open threads' highlight flag, about 13); in the eager bridge, the live part's loader (about 13), the clax:peers case and its SHELL_TYPES entry (about 12), the quotes call in resolveAll (about 12) and making the hook and handing it to comment mode. Removing each was measured; none of it can move to a lazy chunk without the entry or the bridge keeping a call to it. Options: keep these budgets; or refuse and drop a layer (the quote highlight saves about 12 bridge bytes and 13 entry bytes).","kind":"comment","span":{"start":{"line":4},"end":{"line":6},"content_hash":"adfcbbdd6986bbead648210692d9964be604060dac2065973a4d5a5d8a1f532f"},"summary":"Raise or refuse: the live layers' bundle growth (artifact +174, eager bridge +47 gzip bytes over their old budgets; the comment part is back under its own)","supersedes":"f92c2790ce96a3165b773a829005785103f4f41dbe70c6a08100d5063a519595","tags":["live-layers","status:needs-decision","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347","session:claude-code:d1f51555-8e8f-4c11-acd6-673f773ac34d"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/perf/bundle-budget.json","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-22T20:39:37.373973Z","id":"2db52b84aba214ecca8be63108da71e53f909ae0f132f7edac5591ab763f38a8","body":{"detail":"bazelisk test //web:bundle_size at 86ec4f43 measures the artifact entry at 67286 gzip bytes against 67300: the site handshake (web/shell/src/view/artifact-controller.ts redeem, refused, the hs phases) took what removing sandbox mode and the origin probe freed. The next shell addition needs bytes found elsewhere or a raised budget the owner agrees to.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":4},"end":{"line":4},"content_hash":"8d51ec2d5b166166d37d094aeef7284592099ef89fe68bb4ee75240216f546ba"},"summary":"The artifact entry is within 14 bytes of its budget","tags":["bundle","session:claude-code:cc23b85c-a691-4093-ab7a-f909d7a53e66"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/perf/bundle-budget.json","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-22T20:10:35.284282Z","id":"23a551dc4f02fb8086b1b913594e050de0d2b6d498acaa4b2cfd210eee945aa3","body":{"detail":"Moving db, assets and user's request building, subscriptions and asset checks from the shell into the bridge (web/bridge/src/caps/origin-client.ts, origin.ts, asset-checks.ts) and the room's socket (room-socket.ts) measures caps 8191 to 13137 and room 3325 to 4514 (just web-test, bundle_size), while the artifact entry fell 67220 to 62695 and the eager bridge 5541 to 5190, their budgets unchanged. Every page that calls claude.use() now loads the bigger caps part, a comments-only page included.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":9},"end":{"line":10},"content_hash":"7d71af9e62fddaee19b23f62feda4a8fa154fd1413f8f69a1fbbd898f96ff6a2"},"suggested_fix":"Either accept the raise, or split the origin's client and db/assets/user into an `origin` part of its own (parts/, build-parts.mjs, bundle-size.mjs partKeys and a budget of its own), so the shell-served capabilities' pages keep the old caps size.","summary":"partCaps raised 8773 to 13250 and partRoom 3657 to 4600 gzip bytes for the page runtime on the site's origin","tags":["bundle","site-origins","status:needs-decision","session:claude-code:cc23b85c-a691-4093-ab7a-f909d7a53e66"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/perf/bundle-budget.json","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-22T21:11:53.382862Z","id":"446e8e8d480db36c98f656bb1415a6e5024298ae3390d940d1c7778e3fac8fb3","body":{"kind":"comment","references":"23a551dc4f02fb8086b1b913594e050de0d2b6d498acaa4b2cfd210eee945aa3","summary":"Split as decided (da123eb6): the origin's client, db, assets, user and the room's socket are an origin part, loaded only for an origin capability; an unframed page loads no part for a shell capability. just web-test (bundle_size) measures caps 5984 (budget now 6050), origin 9718 (new budget 9850), room 3325 (budget back to 3657), eager bridge 5253 (5548, unchanged), artifact entry 62720 (67300, unchanged). The budget raise this record names is gone; closing it is the owner's.","tags":["bundle","site-origins","session:claude-code:cc23b85c-a691-4093-ab7a-f909d7a53e66"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/perf/bundle-budget.json","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-22T00:27:23.219465Z","id":"9e5732dada691f301f8afcca77647747f275f16c5a9832afcf91a5be1bc4151c","body":{"detail":"web/scripts/bundle-size.mjs measures gallery 30869 and artifact 67412 after the ClaxBot shell work (main measured 30739 and 67271). The gallery's +130: the /admin, /settings, /me and /audit routing in web/shell/src/ui/Gallery.svelte (one regex) and the two NewTile slots. The artifact's +141 comes from no eager code of ClaxBot's: Rollup moved Svelte internals (class and prop helpers) out of the artifact entry into the chunk both entries share (clock-*.js, 138 to 1268 gzip bytes) once the lazy bot/ chunks used them from both entries. Avoiding {@attach}, bind:value on select and <select value=> in web/shell/src/bot kept people (16216) under its 16384 ceiling. Raise or refuse is the owner's call; refusing needs the tile slot and route regex cut from the eager gallery, or a manualChunks rule for Svelte's internals.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":3},"end":{"line":4},"content_hash":"dba5dd194eb37d4b0dbf5b347511e7ff9a8d367df3f9277fada40f95f4c9308a"},"summary":"The gallery and artifact budgets were raised by hand for ClaxBot's web UI (gallery 30800 to 30900, artifact 67300 to 67450)","tags":["status:needs-decision","claxbot","session:claude-code:7580ce1b-abf0-421d-8a2a-2be245f95865"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/perf/bundle-budget.json","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-22T01:42:39.357296Z","id":"18c02ab56ce8d530da74691f1a4f9806aced97f128b30a67ef07e4ec3d33e0de","body":{"kind":"comment","references":"9e5732dada691f301f8afcca77647747f275f16c5a9832afcf91a5be1bc4151c","summary":"Measured after 4a5024bf (bazelisk test //web:bundle_size): gallery 30877, artifact 67397, people 16216, all within the raised budgets of 30900 and 67450 and people's 16384 ceiling.","tags":["session:claude-code:7580ce1b-abf0-421d-8a2a-2be245f95865"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/perf/bundle-budget.json","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-22T15:50:56.415488Z","id":"209469e90aa10a610b5d97705a3e80f488f71c94e03429eb293d8f4435666e0b","body":{"detail":"Measured with node web/scripts/bundle-size.mjs after npm run build: artifact 64243 (budget was 64069), eager bridge 5548 (was 5501; 5462 at 66d2a8f3), comment part 11273 (its budget 11821 kept), the new live part 4197 (budget 4616). The budgets for artifact and bridge are set to those sizes. The drawing, the pointer reports and the quote highlight are the bridge's live part (web/bridge/src/live.ts, loaded by web/bridge/src/live-hook.ts for the first open quote or the first clax:peers naming someone or saying here); the tags, writers, socket and colours load after the first paint with presence (web/shell/src/view/presence-live.ts). What is left: in the entry, the controller's hand-off (web/shell/src/view/artifact-controller.ts startLive, about 70 bytes; react, hello and left, about 20; the clax:cursor/peer-at case, about 19; the open threads' highlight flag, about 13); in the eager bridge, the live part's loader (about 13), the clax:peers case and its SHELL_TYPES entry (about 12), the quotes call in resolveAll (about 12) and making the hook and handing it to comment mode. Removing each was measured; none of it can move to a lazy chunk without the entry or the bridge keeping a call to it. Options: keep these budgets; or refuse and drop a layer (the quote highlight saves about 12 bridge bytes and 13 entry bytes).","kind":"comment","span":{"start":{"line":4},"end":{"line":6},"content_hash":"5293d8b983460dbc0249c88db5cbaad1aed96a38702db043d3472c9b9c054a32"},"summary":"Raise or refuse: the live layers' bundle growth (artifact +174, eager bridge +47 gzip bytes over their old budgets; the comment part is back under its own)","supersedes":"c0e6fdcbbf6e0ad263d1235c883c2ff4ccc468f3227f1b7febc0d72b02b5820c","tags":["live-layers","status:needs-decision","session:claude-code:7580ce1b-abf0-421d-8a2a-2be245f95865"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/perf/bundle-budget.json","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-22T16:57:09.794260Z","id":"cb720cef81a2afc36bbad856b95822518dd18bbd3e1df537cd0e893e96353583","body":{"detail":"web/scripts/bundle-size.mjs calls the questions budget the spec's ceiling and never records it. Rendering a question's text through web/shell/src/ui/Markdown.svelte (7091a44bd) brings the component into the q chunk's imports beyond what the gallery has loaded: questions measured 13,537 before and 17,179 after (bazelisk test //web:bundle_size). The owner prefers raising a budget by a feature's real cost to contorting code; the Markdown module itself (view/markdown.ts) still loads on demand.","kind":"waiver","span":{"start":{"line":6},"end":{"line":6},"content_hash":"f431cb1d3adbb7575951a2a34ca3cb0aa3ab1667f81858fadc38c436e73837d7"},"summary":"The question module's budget is 17,500 gzip bytes, above the 16,384 its spec set, for question text rendered as Markdown","supersedes":"5b52a3653d47183245111febd98d00eef430afe5ce19f8ed07d4b149d5b7bcde","tags":["bundle","session:claude-code:7580ce1b-abf0-421d-8a2a-2be245f95865"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/perf/bundle-budget.json","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-22T16:57:10.679015Z","id":"8d7967bda852f3e92eb44f7a865893aeff9c9974dbb9d878ded6e60a66dfdca2","body":{"detail":"The gallery keeps ClaxBot's growth over main's measured size; the artifact entry fits main's budget, so its raise is gone. Raise or refuse is still the owner's call.","kind":"comment","references":"9e5732dada691f301f8afcca77647747f275f16c5a9832afcf91a5be1bc4151c","summary":"After merge 4f013eec with main: gallery 31047 against 31100 (main's budget was 30936), artifact 68804 against main's 69105 (bazelisk test //web:bundle_size)","tags":["claxbot","bundle","session:claude-code:7580ce1b-abf0-421d-8a2a-2be245f95865"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/perf/budget.json","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-23T21:47:44.852566Z","id":"1eaec0d8ddd91411310313ada133d8491cb4d2fcf3ed3c86b9be0fd6412b39ea","body":{"detail":"Measured 2026-10-13 on one idle Mac (AC power), CLAX_PERF_QUICK=1 npm run perf, main (579bdc8b) and rust-int (5fccef6b) alternating: main comment ready 99-100 ms in run 1 (failed, limit 86 at scale 1.00) and 91 ms in run 2 (passed, limit 94 at scale 1.09); rust-int 101-104 ms in four runs at scale 1.00-1.09 (failed) and 104-128 ms at scale 1.36-1.45 (failed on 128 vs 117). Cold ready latency is also at or over its 38 ms limit on both (39-41 ms). Logs: target/int/ttu-main-*.log and ttu-br-*.log in that worktree. Either the budget no longer matches this machine, or comment readiness regressed before main's tip; the branch adds roughly 3-10 ms on top.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":26},"end":{"line":33},"content_hash":"e298c5613cbfb29022aa4b058349246dd137acc3dac42cd44a81018ae1fe499b"},"summary":"Time to usable's comment ready runs over its 86 ms darwin budget on main and on rust-int alike, the branch a few ms slower","supersedes":"83a2543bcb5633dd4b9f1b963e4fdee6e72091fde7a697b1d3aaf8eb3b6b1d55","tags":["perf","status:needs-decision","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347","session:claude-code:cc23b85c-a691-4093-ab7a-f909d7a53e66"]}}
